		<key>instructionSections</key>
		<array>
			<dict>
				<key>id</key>
				<string>17E5EF71-37E4-5B67-972C-7B7B63187281</string>
				<key>title</key>
				<string>Noodles</string>
				<key>steps</key>
				<array>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>64FE3E02-7034-53F5-A286-A0FD14D1BBFF</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Fill the 8-US-quart pot with cold, fresh water to 1 inch below the top.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>BF2679F0-58CD-5831-B045-4400894666DA</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Salt the water with a heaped tablespoon of salt and bring it to a rolling boil.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>A173A020-6D04-5896-8F64-AC6BAFDB7987</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Add the noodles and cook according to the packet instructions for firm or al dente, usually about 6 minutes.</string>
						<key>duration</key>
						<dict>
							<key>seconds</key>
							<integer>360</integer>
						</dict>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>2F96E42F-3C2D-5238-9A7D-7364C347AF81</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Strain the noodles immediately and transfer them to the baking dish.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>62F6D833-42F7-5FB3-9C5D-D62D20A7CDBF</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Toss the noodles with a bit of olive oil, 2 tablespoons butter, black pepper, Italian seasoning, garlic powder, and onion powder to taste.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>D047CA23-454A-5DFA-A5D5-7ACBCE423A18</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Set the noodles aside while preparing the sauce.</string>
					</dict>
				</array>
			</dict>
			<dict>
				<key>id</key>
				<string>8BD065E0-9914-5051-9768-2B81EB418E76</string>
				<key>title</key>
				<string>Sauce and assembly</string>
				<key>steps</key>
				<array>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>E0591B39-220D-5579-8F2B-1D728EE8DE09</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Preheat the oven to 400°F.</string>
						<key>temperature</key>
						<dict>
							<key>value</key>
							<dict>
								<key>numerator</key>
								<integer>400</integer>
								<key>denominator</key>
								<integer>1</integer>
							</dict>
							<key>unit</key>
							<string>fahrenheit</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>FB03C613-5AE0-5BD6-8638-7EE53B117416</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Finely dice the onions. Sauté them in a generous amount of butter, about 2 tablespoons, seasoning with Montreal steak seasoning, salt, and pepper to taste.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>FC8734E2-5F33-5811-9419-FDB2808CFE38</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Cook until softened or very lightly browned. There is no need for much caramelisation here; the peas will provide ample sweetness.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>BD786987-3060-5464-BCA2-15BD424207DB</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Add the cream of mushroom soup, milk, and tuna. Warm through, then add a dash of Worcestershire sauce and cayenne pepper to taste.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>C769D7A2-EE7F-55A0-A416-A19C8EF095F6</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Taste the sauce. At this point it should be a bit “too much”: just a bit too salty, too savoury, and tuna-forward. It should otherwise be well balanced and look a bit runny. This is ideal; the noodles will absorb and soften the sauce.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>AEB2D6F5-1392-5579-9AA0-754F37227FEB</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Cook just until simmering. CAUTION: It is very easy to burn this sauce! A very gentle fond is nice, but the difference between “fond” and “burned electrical wire” taste is about 15 seconds of high heat, so tame that heat or pay attention.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>825F3A84-851E-5B29-81BC-A681940696E4</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Immediately pour the sauce over the noodles. Add the frozen peas and fold everything together gently.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>28C66830-C5E7-51E0-8DD6-338FBA6C2FD9</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Place the baking dish in the centre of the preheated oven, preferably on a rimmed baking tray to catch possible drips. Check after 10 minutes; the hotdish should just begin to bubble.</string>
						<key>duration</key>
						<dict>
							<key>seconds</key>
							<integer>600</integer>
						</dict>
						<key>temperature</key>
						<dict>
							<key>value</key>
							<dict>
								<key>numerator</key>
								<integer>400</integer>
								<key>denominator</key>
								<integer>1</integer>
							</dict>
							<key>unit</key>
							<string>fahrenheit</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
				</array>
			</dict>
			<dict>
				<key>id</key>
				<string>DF9E54C2-7DB9-5401-B149-D03F8EFFE511</string>
				<key>title</key>
				<string>Topping</string>
				<key>steps</key>
				<array>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>DE1E3A3D-9FB6-5205-9E3A-D1865FA6C16A</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>While the hotdish begins baking, crush the croutons and Ritz crackers into a coarse powder.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>0A401465-AEC3-5751-9C5F-48CE7FE30148</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Melt 2 tablespoons butter and stir it into the topping.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>0356E423-774A-5829-A2F0-380F4D0BA328</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Season with pepper. Salt will not be needed.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>D3BB9CFB-FFFE-579D-A346-90A06B92C250</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Optionally—but highly recommended—grate pecorino into the topping and stir to combine.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>DD50E49B-23B6-5251-8AA1-DFA00BF4F170</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Once the hotdish has begun to bubble, top it evenly and return it to the oven to brown.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>97D48FC3-3F1B-5A50-A655-D06AC5C1A031</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Check after 8 minutes, then every 2 minutes thereafter.</string>
						<key>duration</key>
						<dict>
							<key>seconds</key>
							<integer>480</integer>
						</dict>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>223B1A55-8CF9-508C-BD3A-5640763285A7</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Brown to the desired level and remove promptly.</string>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>id</key>
						<string>A990600A-C643-55D3-B697-FADA006B1620</string>
						<key>text</key>
						<string>Let the hotdish rest for about 10 minutes before serving.</string>
						<key>duration</key>
						<dict>
							<key>seconds</key>
							<integer>600</integer>
						</dict>
					</dict>
				</array>
			</dict>
		</array>
	</dict>
</dict>
